# Canonical author identity.
#
# Every commit in this repository is by one person. The name recorded in the
# commit objects changed over time — the project was called GroundState before
# it was called Bloch, and some commits were made by build and PMO automation
# running under the same author. This file maps all of those to the canonical
# identity, so `git log`, `git shortlog` and `git blame` show one contributor
# instead of six.
#
# It is deliberately a mailmap and not a history rewrite. Rewriting would change
# every commit hash from the genesis commit onward, break every clone, and
# invalidate the dozens of commit references cited in docs/, ADRs and
# post-mortems. The old names in the objects are the record of what actually
# happened; this file is how the record is read, not an edit to it.
#
# Note the one thing it does not do: GitHub's web interface renders the raw
# author from the commit object and does not consult .mailmap, so commits
# already pushed keep displaying their original name there. Git itself, and
# every tool that uses it, honours this file.

Tiago Acioli <tiagobeltraoacioli@gmail.com> Groundstate100 <groundstate100@users.noreply.github.com>
Tiago Acioli <tiagobeltraoacioli@gmail.com> Groundstate100 <founder@posternlabs.com>
Tiago Acioli <tiagobeltraoacioli@gmail.com> Bloch-SIS PoW <bloch-sis-main@proton.me>
Tiago Acioli <tiagobeltraoacioli@gmail.com> Bloch-SIS Protocol <protocol@bloch-sis>
Tiago Acioli <tiagobeltraoacioli@gmail.com> postern-pmo <pmo@posternlabs.com>
Tiago Acioli <tiagobeltraoacioli@gmail.com> postern-build <build@postern.local>

# 2026-09-06: seven more author-name variants found uncovered by the six
# entries above (`git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn`
# on the full, unshallowed history) — all committing under one of the two
# emails already used above, just with a different recorded NAME. The
# single-field form below ("Proper Name <email>", no second bracket group)
# normalizes EVERY commit with that exact email to the given name,
# regardless of what name string the commit object actually recorded — see
# AUTHORS for why these two buckets (same person, same AI tool) are
# consolidated rather than left as apparent separate contributors:
#
#   tiagobeltraoacioli@gmail.com, recorded as one of:
#     "PMO", "perf-bench", "Tiago", "Dev A", "Claude"
#   noreply@anthropic.com, recorded as one of:
